<pre class='metadata'>
Group: AOM
Status: FD
Text Macro: SPECVERSION v2.0.0
Title: Immersive Audio Model and Formats
Editor: SungHee Hwang, Samsung, hshee@samsung.com
Editor: Felicia Lim, Google, flim@google.com
Repository: AOMediaCodec/iamf
Shortname: iamf
URL: https://aomediacodec.github.io/iamf
!Previously approved version: <a href="https://aomediacodec.github.io/iamf/v1.1.0.html">https://aomediacodec.github.io/iamf/v1.1.0.html</a>
!Latest approved version: <a href="https://aomediacodec.github.io/iamf/latest-approved.html">https://aomediacodec.github.io/iamf/latest-approved.html</a>
Date: 2026-08-24
!Reference Implementation: <a href="https://github.com/AOMediaCodec/libiamf">libiamf</a>
Abstract: This document specifies the Immersive Audio (IA) model, the standalone IA Sequence format, and the [[!ISO-BMFF]]-based IA container format. The model represents IA content based on [=Audio Element=]s meant to be rendered and mixed to form one or more presentations. The IA Sequence format, representing IA content, consists of [=Descriptors=] and [=IA Data=]. [=Descriptors=] contain all the information that is required to set up and configure the decoders, renderers, and mixers and [=IA Data=] contains the time-varying data that is needed for the generation of the final IA output. The IA Sequence format supports channel-based, scene-based, and object-based audio formats and the format itself is codec-agnostic but this version of the format supports 4 codecs (OPUS, AAC-LC, FLAC, and LPCM). This document also provides IAMF decoder processing including rendering but the specific rendering algorithm is defined in the <a href="https://www.aomedia.org/specifications/oar/1.0.0/">Open Audio Renderer (OAR)</a> specification.
Local Boilerplate: footer yes
Metadata Order: This version, !*, *
